@1100 = ~ARCHER: The Archer is the epitome of skill with the bow - the ultimate marksman, able to make almost any shot, no matter how difficult. To become so skilled with the bow, the Archer has had to sacrifice some of his proficiency with melee weapons and armor.

Advantages:
- +1 bonus to hit with missile weapons at level 1.
- +1 bonus to hit and damage rolls with any missile weapon at levels 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, and every 4 levels thereafter.
- +1 bonus to Armor Class vs. missile weapons every 6 levels.
- +5% chance to score a critical hit at levels 13 and 18.
- May achieve Grand Mastery (5 slots) in longbows, shortbows, and crossbows.
- Farsighted: +2 visual range, increasing to +4 while hidden or invisible.
- Rapid Shot: While using a bow or crossbow, gains +1 attack per round and suffers a -4 penalty to hit with missile weapons. From level 12 onward, the penalty is reduced to -2.
- Gains one use of Special Shot at level 4 and one additional use every 4 levels thereafter. At level 4, Special Shot may be used to select Called Shot or Rooting Shot. At level 8, Power Shot and Explosive Shot become available as additional choices. Only one Special Shot may be active at a time.
- Called Shot: For the next 10 seconds, every successful ranged attack reduces the target's Dexterity to 50% for 1 turn. At level 8, the target's movement rate is also reduced to 25%. At level 12, the target also loses 1 attack per round. At level 16, the Archer gains +2 missile weapon damage while Called Shot is active. Repeated hits refresh these effects rather than stacking them.
- Manyshot: While using a bow or crossbow, missile damage is increased by 25% at level 7, 40% at level 13, and 60% at level 20.
- Sniper: From level 16 onward, ranged attacks made while invisible or improved invisible are guaranteed critical hits.
- May use the Conjure Elemental Ammunition ability once per day every 8 levels, starting at level 4.
- High-Level Abilities include Greater Called Shot and Sure Shot in addition to the standard Ranger abilities.

Disadvantages:
- Hit Die: d8.
- May not wear any metal armor.
- Suffers a -3 penalty to hit with melee weapons.
- May only become Proficient (one slot) with melee weapons.
- May not place proficiency slots in Two-Weapon Style.
- May not use the Charm Animal ability.
~

@3000 = ~Rapid Shot~
@3001 = ~Rapid Shot
Choose whether to activate or deactivate Rapid Shot. While active, the stance grants +1 attack per round only while a bow or crossbow is equipped, but imposes a -4 penalty to ranged attack rolls. From level 12 onward the penalty is reduced to -2.~
@3002 = ~Activate Rapid Shot~
@3003 = ~Activate Rapid Shot
Enters the Rapid Shot stance. The stance remains active until manually deactivated.~
@3004 = ~Deactivate Rapid Shot~
@3005 = ~Deactivate Rapid Shot
Ends the Rapid Shot stance and removes its attack-rate and ranged accuracy modifiers.~

@3100 = ~Special Shot~
@3101 = ~Special Shot
Select one shot technique. At this level the available techniques are Called Shot and Rooting Shot. All Special Shot techniques consume the same pool of daily uses and cannot be stacked with one another.~
@3102 = ~Special Shot
Select one shot technique. Available techniques are Called Shot, Rooting Shot, Power Shot, and Explosive Shot. All Special Shot techniques consume the same pool of daily uses and cannot be stacked with one another.~

@3200 = ~Called Shot~
@3201 = ~Called Shot
For the next 10 seconds, every successful ranged attack applies the following non-cumulative effects to the target for 1 turn, according to the Archer's level:
4th level: Dexterity is reduced to 50%.
8th level: Movement rate is also reduced to 25%.
12th level: The target also loses 1 attack per round.
16th level: While Called Shot is active, the Archer gains +2 missile weapon damage. This directly increases ranged weapon damage and therefore benefits from critical-hit multipliers.
Repeated hits refresh these effects rather than stacking them.~

@3300 = ~Greater Called Shot~
@3301 = ~Greater Called Shot
For the next 10 seconds, the Archer's base weapon damage is maximized and the Archer gains +2 missile weapon damage. Every successful ranged attack applies the complete Called Shot debuff package to the target and stuns it for 3 seconds. The persistent Called Shot debuffs are refreshed by subsequent hits rather than stacked. Greater Called Shot supersedes and prevents normal Special Shots for its duration.~

@3310 = ~Sure Shot~
@3311 = ~Sure Shot
For 2 rounds, the Archer gains +1 attack per round while a bow or crossbow is equipped, a +4 bonus to ranged attack rolls, and every ranged attack is a critical hit. The concentration required prevents the Archer from moving for the duration.

Activating Sure Shot ends Rapid Shot, normal Special Shots, and Greater Called Shot. These abilities cannot be activated again until Sure Shot ends.

Requires: Critical Strike.~
